(music ends)
(audience cheering)

00:00:01.284 --> 00:00:03.041
- Beautiful.
- Thank you.

00:00:03.041 --> 00:00:07.110
- Okay, and also dialing in from London,

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.496
Adjoa Andoh, give it up for her, y'all!

00:00:09.496 --> 00:00:10.329
(melodic music plays)

00:00:10.329 --> 00:00:13.278
(audience applauds)

00:00:13.278 --> 00:00:17.300
- I mean, geez, you look majestic as well.

00:00:18.216 --> 00:00:19.049
Everybody-
- You look-

00:00:19.049 --> 00:00:19.882
- Adj, you look very lovely.
- Sensational!

00:00:19.882 --> 00:00:21.067
I'm like y'all walked out and I was like,

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.690
"Oh no, I'm underdressed."

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:25.700
And then now I feel very inferior.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:27.980
Adjoa, you look beautiful.
(Adjoa laughs)

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.910
Geez, I am so excited that y'all are here.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:31.920
I don't know if you've heard,

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.820
but I'm like a super fan.
(people laughs)

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.140
And I know you know this
'cause it's your second time

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:36.973
on the show
- It is my second time.

00:00:36.973 --> 00:00:37.982
- But your first time physically-

00:00:37.982 --> 00:00:38.815
- [Nicola] First time in person!

00:00:38.815 --> 00:00:40.659
Last time was from my mom's living room.

00:00:40.659 --> 00:00:42.690
(audience cheers)

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:44.950
- So wait, you posted this on Instagram.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:47.230
So what's happening there?

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:48.063
Let's see this.

00:00:48.063 --> 00:00:49.230
- [Nicola] What's happening here?

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.960
Oh yeah, this was...

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:51.870
Oh my gosh.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.640
- Well, that's you and you.
- That's me and me.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:54.473
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:54.473 --> 00:00:56.740
- Hilariously, I had been
to see Company on Broadway

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.920
with my friend, Camilla,
and we wanted to go

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.450
and get a slice of pizza
cause we were in New York.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:01.917
So we were walking through
Times Square and I was like,

00:01:01.917 --> 00:01:04.213
"La di da di da, oh my God, that's me!"

00:01:04.213 --> 00:01:05.370
And it was like...

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:06.740
It's like 50 foot tall.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.160
No one had told me it was there.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.920
So it was a genuine shock.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.990
So that's actually me
going back another time

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:13.812
to have a look when I'd
slightly composed myself.

00:01:13.812 --> 00:01:15.130
(audience laughing)

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.790
- You're like, "Wait, I
should get footage of it."

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:17.810
Is this like your first time?

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.020
I remember the first time I saw my face

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:19.906
on a billboard and I was like,

00:01:19.906 --> 00:01:20.807
" Wait, what?"
- Yeah.

00:01:20.807 --> 00:01:22.270
I know it's insane.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.688
Just because I didn't know it was there.

00:01:23.688 --> 00:01:25.310
It was such a shock, but-
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:27.086
I feel like they don't tell people.

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:27.919
- [Nicola] No.
(audience laughing)

00:01:27.919 --> 00:01:28.767
- Yeah, it just like happens sometimes.

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:30.320
And you're like, "What?"
- I assume there's a man

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:31.153
from Times Square who's like,

00:01:31.153 --> 00:01:32.923
"Hello, this is Times
Square John, great news!"

00:01:32.923 --> 00:01:35.565
- Great news.
- He does not exist.

00:01:35.565 --> 00:01:37.480
- (laughs) He does not let you know.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:38.840
He does not inform you.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:42.760
Okay, so wait, I have to say
so Charithra and Adjoa, sorry.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:43.660
So what about you two?

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.600
So how have your lives
changed from this show?

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.570
Like being a part of this show.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:50.110
I'll start with you, Adjoa.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:54.950
- Okay, well so I was at the
Queen's platinum Jubilee bash

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:57.040
at Windsor and...

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.424
- As you do.

00:01:58.424 --> 00:01:59.340
(audience laughs)

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.123
- I have a member of the
Royal family asking me,

00:02:03.085 --> 00:02:06.760
you know, "What's coming
next in season three?"

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.700
And then I have a young woman
from Trinidad and Tobago,

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.920
who's in the Air Force over there,

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.840
in the Air Force,
breaking down and weeping

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.830
and saying, "You know,
black girls, we just so...

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:18.840
We love this show."

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.010
So it's just like all ends of the spectrum

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:23.330
are sort of getting involved.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.750
And I was in Atlanta a couple of weeks ago

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.960
and I had a security
guard give me a full on...

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:31.630
A big security guard,
give me a full on curtsy

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:32.620
and wave me through.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:34.427
- [Nicola] Oh my God.
- So, yeah.

00:02:34.427 --> 00:02:35.260
(audience applauding)

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:36.857
It's that kinda stuff, yeah.

00:02:36.857 --> 00:02:38.850
- It's very fitting though, your role.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.490
You look like royalty.
- Yeah, she does.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:43.380
- You came on the screen and
I immediately felt inferior.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:45.770
So like it was... yeah.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:46.760
I love it, you know what though?

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:47.670
It's so true though.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.340
Like so many people from
all different walks of life,

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.210
love this show.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:53.550
It's very rare.
- Yeah.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.887
- That I feel like everybody
joins in on the like,

00:02:55.887 --> 00:02:57.330
"Have you seen the new Bridgerton?

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:58.480
Don't spoil it for me."

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.260
And you know everybody does this.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:01.940
Like how has your life changed?

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:05.440
- I mean, to be honest,
I think I really benefit

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.510
from like wearing masks everywhere

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:09.277
because nobody really recognizes you

00:03:09.277 --> 00:03:10.110
and most of your face
- Me too.

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:11.640
- Is covered up and I love it.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:15.170
'Cause then you get to overhear
people's like real opinions.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:17.160
- Yeah.
- Luckily they've all been,

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.250
You know, positive so far.
- Solid.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.279
- Yeah.

00:03:20.279 --> 00:03:22.870
- But I think I totally
agree with you in that,

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.390
it's kind of...

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:25.840
It's almost like people are surprised

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.470
by how much they enjoy the show.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:30.337
So my housemate, you know, he was like,

00:03:30.337 --> 00:03:32.330
"It wouldn't really be a
show that I would watch

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.078
but I'm gonna watch it for you."

00:03:34.078 --> 00:03:36.740
And so he-
- Cut to he's just like...

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:37.573
- He binges it
(audience laughs)

00:03:37.573 --> 00:03:38.917
and then he was like,

00:03:38.917 --> 00:03:42.350
"This is a really high quality show.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.240
Like I totally see-"
- It's awesome.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.550
- "Why everyone's obsessed."

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:46.490
- Exactly.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:47.323
- So yeah.

00:03:47.323 --> 00:03:49.760
- Yeah, I hate when people
say guilty pleasure.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:50.593
- [Charithra] Yeah, I agree.

00:03:50.593 --> 00:03:52.370
- Cause I'm like, that's
a backhanded compliment.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.203
- Totally-
- Yeah.

00:03:53.203 --> 00:03:54.320
- The things that women
like, they're like, "Oh

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.153
but it's good for them."

00:03:55.153 --> 00:03:56.098
And I'm like,

00:03:56.098 --> 00:03:57.310
"No, it's just good-"
- It's just a pleasure.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:58.310
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:58.310 --> 00:03:59.520
- It's just a pleasure.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.353
- Exactly.

00:04:00.353 --> 00:04:01.720
- A lot of pleasure.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.917
(audience laughs)

00:04:03.917 --> 00:04:04.750
Sometimes.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:06.940
(audience applauding)

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:10.650
So before we talk season
two, I want to ask

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.320
if there's anything you wanted to do

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.430
like while you're in LA.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.090
- Well-
- We had a similar goal.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:17.400
- Yeah, we wanted to-
- What was your goal?

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.010
- Well, to eat Mexican foods.
- Mexican foods.

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:20.120
- Oh.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:21.491
- Yeah, I mean...

00:04:21.491 --> 00:04:22.324
(audience cheers)

00:04:22.324 --> 00:04:23.683
- I love that this was your goal.

00:04:23.683 --> 00:04:24.920
I didn't know that that was...

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.160
We knew that was one of your goals.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.580
I didn't know if there
were, you know, a plethora.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.740
But the one we did know was coming,

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.642
so we wanted to do
something special for y'all.

00:04:32.642 --> 00:04:35.970
So here down, and it's a full on...

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.881
- Ladies, feel free to help
yourselves to the simple trays.

00:04:38.881 --> 00:04:39.714
(audience cheering)

00:04:39.714 --> 00:04:41.337
Feel free help yourselves.
- Oh, we will

00:04:41.337 --> 00:04:42.612
- Help yourselves.
- I know.

00:04:42.612 --> 00:04:43.793
And Justin...

00:04:43.793 --> 00:04:45.584
Oh and margaritas.

00:04:45.584 --> 00:04:46.742
- Are these real?

00:04:46.742 --> 00:04:49.090
- Yes, because-
- Wait, these have tequila?

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.929
- I would toss this on the
floor if it was not real.

00:04:51.929 --> 00:04:52.762
(audience laughs)

00:04:52.762 --> 00:04:55.290
I was like, "They know me, they know me."

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.123
- That's delicious.

00:04:56.123 --> 00:04:59.047
- Cheers ladies-
- On your amazing...

00:04:59.047 --> 00:05:00.540
On your amazing show.
(audience applauds)

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.228
Now I feel bad,

00:05:02.228 --> 00:05:04.220
like Adjoa, I feel bad
that you're not here.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.053
But wait, wait-

00:05:05.053 --> 00:05:07.042
do you have anything there?
- Yeah, feel bad.

00:05:07.042 --> 00:05:08.000
- (laughs) Feel bad.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.960
Yeah, yeah, so Kelly, I was promised

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:13.282
there would be Mexican coming to my door.

00:05:13.282 --> 00:05:14.270
(audience laughs)
Did it come?

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:16.280
No, what have I got in my fridge?

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.403
A carrot.
- Oh!

00:05:18.403 --> 00:05:19.927
- And some Yorkshire cheese.

00:05:19.927 --> 00:05:21.040
- Are you on some kind-
- That's it-

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.370
- Of diet or...
- That would be my equivalent.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:24.647
- Wait I'm not like-
- I know.

00:05:24.647 --> 00:05:25.822
- I'm like, "Wait."

00:05:25.822 --> 00:05:27.280
No, get into it and actually...

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.930
(audience cheers)

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:31.200
Wait, so Justin, what are we...

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.150
What all is this?

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:32.983
So they know.

00:05:32.983 --> 00:05:34.490
Justin's gonna let you
know what everything is.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:37.050
- Yeah, well this is from one
of the best known restaurants

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.850
in Los Angeles it's called Casa Vega.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.181
- [Kelly] Let's go.
(audience applauds)

00:05:40.181 --> 00:05:41.960
- And you guys are actually having

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:44.120
- Oh my God.
- Guacamole fresco,

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.760
chili con queso.
(excited noises)

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.600
A chicken quesadilla.
- Yeah.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.480
- A shrimp quesadilla-
- Let's do the quesadilla-

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.830
corn esquites.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:51.663
- Do you want me to get the-

00:05:51.663 --> 00:05:54.210
- Beef taquitos, con guacamole.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.043
- I love a taquito.
- [Justin] Chicken taquitos,

00:05:55.043 --> 00:05:57.190
day one.
- Big sleeves, big Sleeves.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.925
- El pastor tacos chicos.

00:05:58.925 --> 00:05:59.758
- I wanna try this.

00:05:59.758 --> 00:06:03.280
- Carne Asada tacos chicos, fajitas,

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:06.290
chicken enchiladas, beef enchiladas,

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:08.920
two special oven style burritos.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:09.753
- Oh my gosh.
- Oh my!

00:06:09.753 --> 00:06:11.610
- And margaritas, enjoy!

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:15.596
- [Kelly] So thank you very much.

00:06:15.596 --> 00:06:16.429
Thank you, Justin.

00:06:16.429 --> 00:06:17.340
And also-
- of course.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:19.270
I guess we just really wanted to rub

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.858
that in some more, Adjoa (laughs).

00:06:20.858 --> 00:06:22.017
- I'm sorry-
- Thank you.

00:06:22.017 --> 00:06:24.197
Thank you in detail.

00:06:24.197 --> 00:06:26.920
But I've got a vodka, so it's all good.

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:27.753
- So, it's all good.

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:30.020
Your liquid diet, I like it.
(audience laughs)

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:31.070
So I have to ask-
- Thank you.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:32.450
- Like while you're now chomping down

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:33.584
on some delicious food.
- Do we wanna share?

00:06:33.584 --> 00:06:34.417
I feel bad.

00:06:34.417 --> 00:06:35.250
- I feel like we can't

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.083
'cause of COVID-
- Oh no.

00:06:36.083 --> 00:06:37.830
- But it's a very kind suggestion.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.370
Yeah but just smell it.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.010
Just kinda waft it in

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:43.310
and experience it.
- I feel really bad.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:45.890
Okay, so wait, do y'all
have a favorite moment,

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:47.180
all of you, in season two?

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:48.960
Like I'm gonna be honest with you.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:51.350
When season two came out...

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:52.183
It was about to come out,

00:06:52.183 --> 00:06:55.050
I was like, "This is not gonna
be anything like season one."

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.320
Loved it!

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:58.030
Like it was better than season one

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:00.337
that rarely happens.
- Aww, thank you.

00:07:00.337 --> 00:07:02.670
Rarely happens-
- Thank you.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.370
I loved the new additions.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:05.750
I loved y'all of the sisters coming.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:06.650
I loved all of it.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:07.780
I loved the whole new story.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.270
I loved the diverse cast.

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:10.330
- Mm-hmm
- I loved that.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:12.150
I loved the...

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:14.800
Oh, the tension was nice.
(audience laughs)

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.210
But I'm just curious if y'all
have like a favorite part

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:19.470
of like season two like either
while you were shooting.

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:20.590
Maybe something we
didn't know that happened

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.930
or just a part of the show.

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:26.720
- Ooh, I think my favorite scene to shoot

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:29.770
from season two was the
haldi scene in episode six.

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:30.603
Just because, you know,

00:07:30.603 --> 00:07:34.540
I think you never really know
how people are gonna react

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:35.640
to certain scenes, right?

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.740
Like you hope for the best
and you can feel passionate.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:40.400
But when we were filming that scene,

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.920
I think all of us, including
the crew, felt this sense

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:46.460
of like, "Oh my goodness,
we're kind of making history."

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:48.380
I don't think we've ever seen something

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:49.890
like this on screen before...

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:50.723
- Yeah.

00:07:50.723 --> 00:07:53.560
- And it looked very different
to other scenes in the show.

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:57.010
And so it's really special to me

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:59.090
'cause it just feels so monumental.

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:01.301
- Yeah, something like
new and fresh as well.

00:08:01.301 --> 00:08:02.705
That should have been happening.

00:08:02.705 --> 00:08:04.310
(audience cheers)
Yeah, I like that.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:05.230
What's your favorite?

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.540
- I mean, I have to...

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:08.540
I always love dancing with Luke Newton.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:10.326
He's so cute-
(audience cheering)

00:08:10.326 --> 00:08:11.867
- [Kelly] I love him.

00:08:11.867 --> 00:08:13.440
- But he is like the best dancer

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:14.970
'cause he's musical theater trained.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:16.700
So that boy can sing, dance, act,

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:17.620
he can do it all.
- Oh he is like one

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.340
of those old school movie stars.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:20.650
- Oh, 100%, yeah.
- I don't think I'm allowed

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:22.620
to say old school anymore
but I just did it.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:23.830
- He just sent me a picture of him,

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:26.180
I have to show it to you, for
a fitting for season three

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.702
and, "Oh my gosh." (laughs)

00:08:27.702 --> 00:08:28.561
(audience cheering)
It's really...

00:08:28.561 --> 00:08:31.370
I like felt very weird, I
was like, "Luke!" (laughs)

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:33.410
- Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:34.590
So you're just like already

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:35.440
filming season three.
- We're already

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:36.900
in fittings, no, we're not filming yet.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:37.870
But the fittings take a long time

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:39.750
'cause they make everything custom.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:40.583
Literally every single garment

00:08:40.583 --> 00:08:41.808
that we wear.
- Oh my God.

00:08:41.808 --> 00:08:43.200
I fluctuate like so much.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:44.910
Like does that work out?

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:45.820
- I said, I was like, "You know,

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:47.130
what if I like become a bodybuilder?"

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:49.000
They were like, "That's
chill, we'll work around you."

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.480
- Or if you like, yeah, lose it again.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:53.410
I literally like from like
morning to trying on an outfit

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:54.850
for this show to like the afternoon,

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:56.950
it will either be like a huge sack on me

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.850
or like, "When did this
ever fit so tight?"

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.497
- Oh, I tried a shoe on
yesterday and I was like,

00:09:00.497 --> 00:09:01.350
"That is not my foot."

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.240
And I was like, "I was flying," (laughs)

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:05.240
looking at the foot.
- I know and it swells.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:06.928
That's a turd of a thing that happens.

00:09:06.928 --> 00:09:09.658
So yes, I don't know why I said turd.

00:09:09.658 --> 00:09:13.260
So Adjoa, what's your favorite
part like of season two?

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.850
- I guess I got...

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:18.730
I love the balls because I like watching

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:22.650
the floor manager and the
director try and wrangle

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:28.170
over exhausted, overexcited,
eaten too much sugar,

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.380
grown up children.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.450
It's like a classroom of four year olds

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:35.520
at 5:00 in the morning
and it's like, "Take 982."

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:37.930
And you've been in your
corset for 12 hours

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.240
and everybody's just behaving badly.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.540
So I love that stuff.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:45.300
I loved the scene I did with Ruth Gemmell

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:48.870
who plays Lady Violet when
we both were just laughing.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:51.310
The laughy scenes, 'cause I just...

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:53.530
I like laughing and I
like laughing with Ruth

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:54.970
and we usually get in trouble for it.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:57.260
But there was actually
a scene written for us

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.400
to do proper laughing.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.143
And so that was

00:10:00.143 --> 00:10:00.976
really good fun
- [Kelly] Getting paid for it.

00:10:00.976 --> 00:10:04.510
And then watching these two
girls you've got on there.

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:05.343
- Yeah.

00:10:05.343 --> 00:10:09.350
And Simone watching those
girls dancing, oh my...

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:12.945
And it doesn't matter
how many takes you do,

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:14.323
they are so on it-
(audience applauds)

00:10:14.323 --> 00:10:16.030
they are just brilliant.

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:18.010
So it's beautiful to just watch.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:20.500
- So Charithra, social media has praised

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:22.390
casting darker skinned Indian actors.

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.570
So what has this meant for you?

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:26.660
- Colorism has existed

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:29.520
at different times throughout history.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:33.610
And I think it is particularly
pervasive in countries

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:37.075
in Asia and in Africa and
south Asia and east Asia

00:10:37.075 --> 00:10:40.110
because of, well, one colonialism

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.180
and second to do with class and caste.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:45.820
And so, you know, it's a daily struggle

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:47.730
for us 'cause we're never
allowed to forget it.

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:50.350
And I always say it feels kind of violent

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:53.370
to me because it comes from
within your own community.

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:54.203
- Yeah.

00:10:54.203 --> 00:10:56.870
And so I just hope that Simone and I being

00:10:56.870 --> 00:11:01.295
in the show can help dark
skinned people of all races

00:11:01.295 --> 00:11:03.930
to feel beautiful and to feel seen

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:05.434
and to feel worthy of love.

00:11:05.434 --> 00:11:06.958
- Yeah, absolutely.
- Yeah.

00:11:06.958 --> 00:11:08.100
(audience cheers)

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.430
- And it's also like one of my...

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:11.120
We love the artwork by the way.

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:12.090
And when people dress up,

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:12.940
we love it.
- Oh my God.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:15.100
- And one of my favorite ones

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:18.450
is of these two children who were dressed

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:20.550
up as the Duke and Lady Danbury.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:21.383
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:11:21.383 --> 00:11:24.390
- And I'm like growing up, I
didn't know who to dress up

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:25.780
for Halloween parties.
- Exactly, yeah.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:27.420
- I felt ridiculous dressing up

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:29.160
as Cinderella or Sleeping Beauty,

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:32.530
I was so scared people
would ask me who I was

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:34.430
even though I obviously was Belle.

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:35.263
- Yeah.
- You know?

00:11:35.263 --> 00:11:38.580
And so for young girls
to be able to dress up

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:41.590
as a Dowager and a Duke and you know

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:44.290
a princess and all of
these things is amazing.

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:45.330
- Adjoa you were talking

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:47.170
about how important it was
for you as well, right?

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:49.800
And you were having women come
up to you and talk to you?

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:54.150
- Listen, I can't tell you, it's...

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.630
As Charithra was saying,

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:59.590
when little boys and girls
dress up as Lady Danbury,

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:01.940
which they do and send me their pictures,

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.960
I just...

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.637
When I was a kid, you would
run to the television,

00:12:06.637 --> 00:12:07.716
"There's a black person on the television.

00:12:07.716 --> 00:12:08.890
Come on, come on, come on!"

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:10.290
You'd be like, "Oh."

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:12.570
But, so I am thrilled.

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:15.020
But I'm also thrilled,
you know, if you are gay,

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:16.260
you can watch this show.

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:18.470
If you are a woman who
wants to be a homemaker

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:20.150
or a woman who wants an independent life

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:21.300
you can watch this show.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.520
Or you can just watch this show

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:26.280
'cause you like a nice, you
know, 18th century frock

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.240
or a stately home, or you wanna see a bit

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:29.560
of will they won't they.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:33.000
Whatever your particular thing is,

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.370
you can watch our show and know

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:35.550
that you are welcome.
- Yeah.

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:36.760
- That it's a wide embrace.

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:40.190
And it's a show that says,
"Everybody is just a person.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:41.570
And sometimes we do great things

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.400
and sometimes we do terrible things,

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:47.620
but we are all frail, and
we all want to be loved

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:48.470
and we all want to be seen

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:50.930
and we want to be heard,
come and watch our show.

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:52.164
You're welcome."
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:12:52.164 --> 00:12:52.997
- That's what I love about it.

00:12:52.997 --> 00:12:53.830
(audience cheers)

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:56.280
- That was like the best tease ever

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:57.600
for a show.
- I know.

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:59.230
Yeah, I love that, I love that.

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:00.810
And I fully believe in that as well.

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:03.230
So the casting has been widely praised.

00:13:03.230 --> 00:13:04.800
Here are a couple of the reactions.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:08.660
One person tweeted, " So happy
to see dark skin Indian women

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:11.410
playing female leads in
Bridgerton, season 2.

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:15.060
Thank you, they don't even
do this in Tamil cinemas."

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:18.197
And here is what another
person posted as well,

00:13:18.197 --> 00:13:22.080
"Indian culture is beautiful,
vibrant and welcoming

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.980
and yet so often ignored.

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:26.610
So when I saw this scene in the trailer,

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:29.180
as an Indian American
teen, I was beyond proud,

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:31.181
grateful, and honored,
thank you Bridgerton."

00:13:31.181 --> 00:13:34.340
I feel like that's gotta make you feel...

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:36.100
All of you, just feel so proud.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:36.959
That's you're like representing
something different-

00:13:36.959 --> 00:13:38.540
- It's amazing, that's the
kind of work you want to make.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:39.373
- Yeah, exactly.

00:13:39.373 --> 00:13:41.800
- Because art is about
expressing the real world

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:42.750
in a beautiful way.

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.347
And it's like, you know, you
can watch the show and go,

00:13:44.347 --> 00:13:45.640
"It's lovely and it's
colorful and it's fun."

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:48.120
But like what it's done
has been so amazing.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:49.210
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- It's been so amazing

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:50.180
And when we got to go...

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:51.710
I don't know why I'm getting so emotional.

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:53.280
But when we went to the
Bridgerton experience

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:55.130
the other night and seeing people

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:58.100
of all shapes, sizes, colors
there celebrating the joy

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.000
that this show has brought them.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.080
It like really touched a nerve.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:01.913
It's so beautiful,

00:14:01.913 --> 00:14:03.722
we feel really privileged.
(audience cheers)

00:14:03.722 --> 00:14:06.000
- You're gonna make me cry,
I'm like a contagious crier.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:08.880
So what are you doing to me, Nicola?

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:10.430
I know, I'm like, "Oh my gosh,

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:12.570
she's gonna make me cry."
- Yeah, it's so lovely.

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:15.069
- So I think that that is the
most amazing thing as well.

00:14:15.069 --> 00:14:15.902
- Yeah.

00:14:15.902 --> 00:14:16.735
I do hope...

00:14:16.735 --> 00:14:21.120
I guess my hope is that
one day it's not so rare.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:21.953
You know what I'm saying?

00:14:21.953 --> 00:14:23.130
And it's not an innovative thing

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:26.940
and it's not a person running
to the TV going," Oh my God!

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:27.773
Someone that looks like me."

00:14:27.773 --> 00:14:28.606
You know what I'm saying?

00:14:28.606 --> 00:14:30.900
Like I have a little
boy that loves to dress

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:31.733
up like a princess.

00:14:31.733 --> 00:14:32.566
He's like...

00:14:32.566 --> 00:14:34.780
I mean, he'll be a ninja
as well but like he loves

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:35.780
to dress up like Ariel.

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:37.310
And in my house that's like, totally fine.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:38.410
Whatever you wanna dress up as.

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:42.150
And I think that that's
all really important

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:43.780
and I feel like it's 2022.

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:46.080
And we should just like what you said,

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:48.280
it's about, we're all the same.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:49.780
We all bleed red, we all wanna be loved.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:50.900
We all wanna be a part of this story.

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:52.483
We all wanna have a seat at the table.

00:14:52.483 --> 00:14:54.860
- And it's also like
about different displays

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:56.770
of power and strength.

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:58.440
'Cause it's like, especially
with your character,

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:02.460
it's like, she's such a complex person

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.450
and mine too.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:06.500
- Our displays of
strength are so different

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:09.990
from like what's been the
standard for so long, right?

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:13.760
Like women often they've
been told to be strong,

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:15.450
you've got to be really outspoken

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:19.350
and bold and you know,
an extrovert really.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:23.260
When the reality is that's
only one form of it.

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:24.410
- Totally, yeah-
And I hope that...

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:26.597
Like so many women have
come up to you and gone,

00:15:26.597 --> 00:15:28.280
"I'm so a Penelope."
- So a Penelope.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.113
- Yeah.

00:15:29.113 --> 00:15:29.946
- And it's so sweet.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:15:29.946 --> 00:15:30.947
For years, you used to
get scripts, where like,

00:15:30.947 --> 00:15:32.360
"She's this guy's girlfriend."

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.400
And you go, "What woman that you know

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:35.530
is just this guy's girlfriend?

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:36.660
That's not a thing."

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:37.493
- Yeah.

00:15:37.493 --> 00:15:38.900
- You know, we're all
fully rounded human beings.

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:39.980
And this show like makes...

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:42.610
And our characters, they
do unlikable things.

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:43.708
You know, but like you have-

00:15:43.708 --> 00:15:44.541
- We're women
- To allow it.

00:15:44.541 --> 00:15:45.640
- And we do unlikable things.

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:47.220
- Exactly, I always make the joke.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.160
I always say like, no
one watched Breaking Bad

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:50.480
and they're like, "Let's make Walter White

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:53.220
like a little softer, so he
is like a little more..."

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.415
- Yeah.
- You know what I mean?

00:15:54.415 --> 00:15:55.700
(Kelly laughs)

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:56.910
Like, "He's just not very relatable.

00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:57.832
We don't like root for him."

00:15:57.832 --> 00:15:59.640
But like, you know-
- He's not very relatable.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:00.510
Could you please

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:01.627
like tone him down?
- Yeah, just put him

00:16:01.627 --> 00:16:03.744
in a little nice, little jumper
that's a bit more, you know.

00:16:03.744 --> 00:16:05.935
We would never do that.
(Kelly laughs)

00:16:05.935 --> 00:16:06.821
We would never do that

00:16:06.821 --> 00:16:07.960
- [Charithra] Yeah.
- Oh my God,

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:09.743
that was the greatest analogy.

00:16:09.743 --> 00:16:12.830
So wait, Adjoa, what's
going on with season three?

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:14.083
What's happening?

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:17.530
- Well, it's gonna get twisty.

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:18.789
It's certainly gonna get twisty.

00:16:18.789 --> 00:16:19.622
- [Charithra] Oh yeah.

00:16:19.622 --> 00:16:21.300
Do you know the way as
you were saying Kelly,

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:23.540
like you loved season
one and then season two

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:26.040
had its own extra level of...

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.750
Season three's gonna
have an extra level of...

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:29.640
Trust me.

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:34.320
So you'll see more
complicated relationships.

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:37.210
There will be people from
people's pasts turning up

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:38.910
in new and exciting ways.

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:43.080
And yeah, I think if you love season two,

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:45.140
then I think you should get really excited

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:46.667
about season three.

00:16:46.667 --> 00:16:47.500
(audience applauds)

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:48.667
- Okay, so it's time for another break.

00:16:48.667 --> 00:16:50.810
Adjoa, we know it's late in London

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:52.550
so we are gonna let you get some sleep.

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:53.383
Thank you so much

00:16:53.383 --> 00:16:55.553
for looking so fabulous.
- [Nicola] Love you, Adj.

00:16:55.553 --> 00:16:56.811
- You look so fabulous.

00:16:56.811 --> 00:16:57.644
Thank you so much for calling in.

00:16:57.644 --> 00:16:58.953
I love this show-

